Third-party material
--------------------

Upstream projects. Each case Dockerfile (bench/cases/*/Dockerfile, chainlab/cases/*/Dockerfile)
downloads the affected upstream project at build time, from GitHub's codeload service at a pinned
commit or from PyPI/npm at a pinned version. That upstream code is NOT redistributed in this
repository; it stays under its own licence. File paths, line numbers, symbol names and commit
SHAs of upstream projects appear in case metadata only to identify the vulnerable code.

GitHub Advisory Database. Advisory identifiers, titles and summaries quoted in case metadata,
docs/MANIFEST.md, docs/advisory-status.json and paths-to-root/ come from the GitHub Advisory
Database (https://github.com/advisories), which is licensed under CC BY 4.0.

Semgrep rules. Semgrep registry rule packs are licensed under the Semgrep Rules License and are NOT
included. bench/tools/semgrep/SNAPSHOT.json records only the pack names and the sha256 of the
snapshot used for the v0 scores.

Base images. Case Dockerfiles reference public base images (for example python and node official
images) pinned by digest or version tag. They are pulled from their registries at build time and are not
redistributed here.

Deliberately vulnerable code. The case images reproduce known, already-fixed vulnerabilities on
purpose. Build and run them only through bench/run.py or chainlab/run.py, which isolate them.
